    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes, you can.  Digi-Egg cards in the battle area and breeding area are treated as Digimon, so they can be trashed.",
        "question": "Can I use this card's [Main] effect to trash 1 Digi-Egg card in the breeding area?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, you can't.  You must perform both \"deleting 1 of your [Ukkomon] and trashing 1 of your Digimon in the breeding area\" to play a [BigUkkomon] into the breeding area.",
        "question": "Can I perform just \"deleting 1 of your [Ukkomon]\" or \"trashing 1 of your Digimon in the breeding area\" to play a [BigUkkomon] into the breeding area for this card's [Main] effect?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, the effect reads “you may play.\"",
        "question": "After performing \"deleting 1 of your [Ukkomon]\" and \"trashing 1 of your Digimon in the breeding area,\" can I choose to not play a [BigUkkomon] into the breeding area for this card's [Main] effect?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it's processed.  \nOverflow is processed when a card is sent from the area or from under a card to another area. In this case, it's processed because a card from the area is placed in the trash.",
        "question": "Is \nOverflow processed when this card's [Main] effect trashes a Digimon with \nOverflow in the breeding area?",
        "reference": "[2]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it's processed.  \nOverflow is processed when a card is sent from the area or from under a card to another area. In this case, it's processed because it's placed into the trash from under a card.",
        "question": "Is \nOverflow processed when this card's [Main] effect trashes a Digimon in the breeding area that has a card with \nOverflow in its digivolution cards?",
        "reference": "[2]"
      }
    ]
  },
